# Checkbox

<h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>

A checkbox lets people choose none, one or several options, or set a single preference that is saved with a form. It records an answer. It does not send a command to a device.

This page covers:

- Checkbox
  - `<input type="checkbox">`
  - `ha-checkbox`

<h2 id="anatomy">Anatomy</h2>

1. A small box that is empty, ticked or, in a long list, partly ticked.
2. A label next to it. The whole label is part of the click target.
3. An optional hint under the label.
4. For a group, a legend that asks the question, with a hint if it helps.

<h2 id="variants">Variants, variables and extensibility</h2>

<h3 id="child-input-type-checkbox"><code>&lt;input type="checkbox"&gt;</code></h3>

The browser’s own checkbox. It has `checked`, `disabled`, `required`, `name` and `value`, which is “on” unless you set it. Pressing Space toggles it. Enter does not. A value is sent only when the box is ticked. A partly ticked state exists only as a visual mark and is never sent.

Give it a visible label, either wrapped round it or joined to it. Put related boxes in a fieldset with a legend.

<h3 id="child-ha-checkbox"><code>ha-checkbox</code></h3>

The Home Assistant checkbox, which appears in editors, lists and dialogs rather than as a dashboard card. The label is the default content and the hint goes in the `hint` slot.

It has these attributes: `checked`, `disabled`, `indeterminate`, `required` and `variant`. The variants are `brand` (the default), `neutral`, `success`, `warning` and `danger`. The box is 20px, with a minimum touch size of 40px.

What Civica sets, in the light and dark themes:

- Border: `ha-color-border-neutral-normal`, `#6F777B` and `#9BA4AA`. The border is 2px wide (`ha-border-width-md`). On hover it uses `ha-color-border-neutral-loud`.
- Unticked background: `wa-form-control-background-color`, `#FFFFFF` and `#24282B`. On hover it uses `ha-color-form-background-hover`.
- Ticked background: `ha-color-fill-primary-loud-resting`, `#1D70B8` and `#C0D7EB`, and `#195C96` and `#D6E5F2` on hover.
- Variant fills: `ha-color-fill-success-loud-resting`, `ha-color-fill-warning-loud-resting` and `ha-color-fill-danger-loud-resting`, each with a light and a dark value.
- Focus ring: 3px wide, offset 2px, black in the light theme and yellow in the dark theme.

What Civica leaves as Home Assistant’s default: the size, the corner radius and the colour of the tick. The corners stay slightly rounded. You can make them square by adding `--ha-checkbox-border-radius: 0` to the theme, but Civica does not set it. The theme’s older `mdc-checkbox-*` keys apply only to older checkboxes, not to this one. Test the focus ring on this checkbox in your own dashboard.

<h3 id="label-and-hint">Label and hint</h3>

The label and the hint belong inside `ha-checkbox`, as its default content and its `hint` slot.

For an immediate on or off, such as a lamp, use a switch instead. A checkbox is for an answer that is saved or submitted later.

<h2 id="limits">Advantages and limitations</h2>

- A checkbox group is clear for several independent choices.
- The browser checkbox works without the Home Assistant frontend and needs no extra code.
- A dashboard author cannot place `ha-checkbox` as a card. It appears in Home Assistant’s own forms and lists.
- The tick colour, size and corner radius are not set by the theme, so they stay as Home Assistant draws them.
- Test the colour and contrast of the box against its background in your own dashboard.

<h2 id="usage">Usage policy and cognitive accessibility</h2>

Use a group when several rooms can be included in a view. Use one checkbox for a reversible preference, such as showing hidden rooms. Do not use a group for a single choice such as temperature units; use [Radios](radios.html). Do not use a checkbox to run a device. Ticking a room in a filter must not switch its devices on.

- Group related boxes in a [Fieldset](fieldset.html) with a legend.
- Show a saved preference as it was saved. For a new question, do not tick an answer for the person.
- Say whether several choices are allowed.
- If you add a “none of these” option, enforce it when the form is submitted as well as on the page.
- Keep labels short and make the whole label a generous target.

Success criteria that apply:

- 1.3.1 Info and Relationships: the label is joined to the box.
- 2.1.1 Keyboard: Space toggles it.
- 2.5.8 Target Size (Minimum): `ha-checkbox` declares a 40px minimum touch size.
- 3.2.2 On Input: ticking a box must not change the page unexpectedly.
- 3.3.2 Labels or Instructions and 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value.

Test Space, saved values, no selection, long room names and touch targets, in light and dark modes and at 320 CSS pixels. See [Test the interface](../accessibility/testing.html).

